.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

node_modules/
web/dist/
.vite/

# ── What is and is not committed under data/ ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Dataset OUTPUTS are committed, so the app is clone-and-run with no API pull.
# Everything under data/raw/ is an INPUT and is ignored wholesale, because every
# one is re-fetchable by re-running the step that reads it:
#
#   data/raw/cache/   the polite-fetch HTTP cache. Scratch by definition.
#   data/raw/geo/     Natural Earth downloads, ~55 MB. The committed artifacts
#                     are web/public/geo/, built by scripts/build_geo.mjs.
#   data/raw/golden/  recorded runs for the golden master.
#
# The rule is deliberately the whole directory rather than a list. In the atlas
# this was forked from an earlier version listed only two subdirectories, and
# 28 MB of zips were committed before anyone noticed: a per-directory allowlist
# fails open, which is the wrong direction for a rule about repository weight.
data/raw/

# Vite dev/build artefacts under web/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# ── Live vessel positions (docs/PLAN.md, T13) ─────────────────────────────────
# The aisstream.io key, and any snapshot a future collector writes.
.env
web/public/data/vessels/

# Frames and receipts the runner writes (atlas/run.py). Always rebuildable.
build/

# TypeScript incremental build state; rebuilt by `tsc -b`.
web/*.tsbuildinfo
